{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nusing lint = long long;\n\nconst lint MOD = 1000000007;\n\nlint fast_pow(lint base, lint exp) {\n    lint res = 1;\n    while (exp) {\n        if (exp & 1) res = (res * base) % MOD;\n        base = (base * base) % MOD;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nstruct DisjointSet {\n    vector<int> root;\n    vector<int> depth;\n    int component_count;\n\n    DisjointSet(int n) : root(n), depth(n), component_count(n) {\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) root[i] = i;\n    }\n\n    int find(int x) {\n        if (root[x] != x) root[x] = find(root[x]);\n        return root[x];\n    }\n\n    void connect(int x, int y) {\n        x = find(x), y = find(y);\n        if (x == y) return;\n        if (depth[x] > depth[y]) swap(x, y);\n        root[x] = y;\n        if (depth[x] == depth[y]) depth[y]++;\n        component_count--;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    lint p, k;\n    cin >> p >> k;\n\n    vector<int> visited(p);\n    DisjointSet dsu(p);\n\n    for (lint i = 0; i < p; ++i) {\n        for (lint j = i; !visited[j]; j = (j * k) % p) {\n            visited[j] = 1;\n            dsu.connect(i, j);\n        }\n    }\n\n    int result_components = dsu.component_count;\n    if (k != 1) result_components--;\n\n    cout << fast_pow(p, result_components) << '\\n';\n\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\ndef fast_pow(base, exp, MOD=1000000007):\n    res = 1\n    while exp:\n        if exp & 1:\n            res = (res * base) % MOD\n        base = (base * base) % MOD\n        exp >>= 1\n    return res\n\nclass DisjointSet:\n    def __init__(self, n):\n        self.root = list(range(n))\n        self.depth = [0] * n\n        self.component_count = n\n    \n    def find(self, x):\n        if self.root[x] != x:\n            self.root[x] = self.find(self.root[x])\n        return self.root[x]\n    \n    def connect(self, x, y):\n        x = self.find(x)\n        y = self.find(y)\n        if x == y:\n            return\n        if self.depth[x] > self.depth[y]:\n            x, y = y, x\n        self.root[x] = y\n        if self.depth[x] == self.depth[y]:\n            self.depth[y] += 1\n        self.component_count -= 1\n\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    p = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    \n    visited = [0] * p\n    dsu = DisjointSet(p)\n    \n    for i in range(p):\n        j = i\n        while not visited[j]:\n            visited[j] = 1\n            dsu.connect(i, j)\n            j = (j * k) % p\n    \n    result_components = dsu.component_count\n    if k != 1:\n        result_components -= 1\n    \n    print(fast_pow(p, result_components))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00013517419574782252, -7.152555099310121e-07, 0.0, -0.4718383848667145, -0.009852588